            <div class="journalistic-interview">
                <p id="int-intro" class="interview-intro-text">
                    For decades, Fairchild has stood at the forefront of tropical plant research and environmental stewardship. The pressing challenge today is uniting science, public gardens, and community action to counter biodiversity loss.
                </p>

                <div class="qa-card-modern">
                    <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-seedling"></i> <span id="q1-title">Biodiversity Under Pressure</span></h4>
                    <p id="q1-desc">Subtropical ecosystems face intense pressures from invasive species and rapid urban development. Protecting native flora requires proactive field conservation and advanced laboratory propagation.</p>
                    <div class="verbatim-quote" id="v1">
                        "Plant diversity is the foundation of all terrestrial life. Losing even one native species can trigger a cascading effect throughout the local ecosystem."
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="qa-card-modern">
                    <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-water"></i> <span id="q2-title">Water Resources and Wetlands</span></h4>
                    <p id="q2-desc">South Florida's unique hydrological landscape makes water management critical for both human populations and natural habitats under climate stress.</p>
                    <div class="verbatim-quote" id="v2">
                        "Water is life in South Florida. Balancing urban needs with the natural flow of our wetlands is essential for long-term ecological survival."
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="qa-card-modern">
                    <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-tree"></i> <span id="q3-title">Urban Greening and Reintroduction</span></h4>
                    <p id="q3-desc">Projects like the Million Orchid Project demonstrate how urban areas can actively support ecological restoration by returning native species back into our cities.</p>
                    <div class="verbatim-quote" id="v3">
                        "When we bring nature back into our urban centers, we reconnect people with the environment right outside their doors."
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="qa-card-modern">
                    <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-bridge"></i> <span id="q4-title">Education and Community Action</span></h4>
                    <p id="q4-desc">Empowering the next generation through citizen science ensures that conservation values translate into lifelong environmental stewardship.</p>
                    <div class="verbatim-quote" id="v4">
                        "Education is our strongest tool. When students touch, study, and protect plants, they become lifelong advocates for the planet."
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

